Makes FolderState::restarted clear the batch window and leave it closed
again, as before e06de00 (§11): the window lives in memory and dies with the
process, while the records it was about to announce survive in the index,
and without the fix they wait for this node's next local write instead of
going out at the next tick. The `now` argument e06de00 added stays, unused,
so that no caller changes. No seed in 0 to 9,999 fails with this patch, and
the one seed at 2,000 steps that does fails indirectly and will not shrink
below 1,217 steps, so the patch names the rule's unit test.

test: delocal-engine engine::tests::a_restart_reopens_the_window_for_unannounced_records

